  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q25-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": "Five dice are rolled and the product of the numbers is recorded. Find the probability that the result is a multiple of 25.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{763}{3888}$.\n\nThe product is a multiple of 25 exactly when at least two dice show 5; subtract the probabilities of zero and exactly one five.",
      "worked": "Only a roll of 5 contributes a factor of 5, so the product is a multiple of 25 exactly when at least two dice show 5. Let $A$ be this event. Its complement consists of no fives or exactly one five. There are five possible positions for the single five.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{no fives})&=\\left(\\frac56\\right)^5\\\\\\Pr(\\text{exactly one five})&=5\\times\\frac16\\times\\left(\\frac56\\right)^4\\\\\\Pr(A)&=1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^5-5\\times\\frac16\\times\\left(\\frac56\\right)^4\\\\\\Pr(A)&=1-\\frac{3125}{7776}-\\frac{3125}{7776}\\\\\\Pr(A)&=\\frac{763}{3888}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
